{
 "_about": "Distinct senses of a kanji, each written as a group of accepted wordings with the one to teach listed first. KANJIDIC2's gloss list is not a list of senses: it mixes genuinely different meanings (月 = Month, Moon) with plain synonyms (大 = Large, Big) and with wordings nobody would type (対 = 'Vis-a-vis'). Grouping them fixes two things at once.",
 "_fixes": "1) The sense ladder stops spending a card teaching 'Big' as the second meaning of 大, because 大 has one sense here, not two. 2) Typed answers can be graded against the primary sense strictly while still accepting every reasonable wording of it, which is what makes strict grading fair enough to switch on.",
 "_format": "senses[kanji] = [ [sense 1 wordings...], [sense 2 wordings...] ]. The first wording in each group is the one taught and shown. Any wording in the group counts as fully correct for that sense. Kanji absent from this file fall back to the raw gloss list.",
 "_scope": "Curated across the beginner range -- the top ~150 by newspaper frequency plus all of Grade 1 -- because that is where the noise actually costs a learner something. Kanji whose raw glosses were already correct are curated too, since strict grading only applies where groupings exist. It is a judgment call and meant to be corrected: copy an entry into userdata/senses.local.json to override it, same as spoken.local.json.",
